> So, just to be sure: if for example I eat something poisonous, could I
> use my horn 100 turns later to recover the lost strength?
>
Maybe.  If you lose an attribute, a unicorn horn can restore that
attribute back up to its pre-loss state, unless you happen to gain
that attribute back (in whole or in part) another way.
For example, you eat something poisonous and lose 1 STR.  Then you
happen to exercise your strength and gain 1 str.  At that point a
unicorn horn will not give you an additional point of strength.  What
I can not remember is what happens if you lose 2 points of str and
exercise gives you 1 back, and then you apply your horn, but I think
you will then gain 1 point of str and be back where you started.
AFAIK there is no timeout for stat loss recovery and I seem to
remember eating poisonous corpses as a XL=1 and then having to wait
until XL=8 (or whatever) to find my first unicorn horn and recover the
strength.

